  "estimatedMinutes": 1,
  "statement": "A straight line passing through the point \\((0,4)\\) is perpendicular to the line \\(x-3y-7=0.\\) Its equation is:",
  "answerChoices": [
    {
      "label": "A",
      "text": "\\(y+3x-4=0\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "B",
      "text": "\\(y+3x+4=0\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "C",
      "text": "\\(y-3x-4=0\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "D",
      "text": "\\(3y+x-12=0\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "E",
      "text": "\\(3y-x-12=0\\)"
    }
  ],
  "answer": {
    "letter": "a",
    "value": null
  },
  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.ahsme-1968-p3.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "The given line has slope \\(\\frac{1}{3},\\) so a perpendicular line has slope \\(-3.\\) Through \\((0,4)\\) its equation is \\(y=-3x+4,\\) or \\(y+3x-4=0.\\)\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is A.",
      "hints": [
        "The given line has slope \\(\\frac{1}{3}\\)",
        "Use the negative reciprocal slope through \\((0,4)\\)"
      ],
      "images": []
    }
  ],
